      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/r/71e660/{size}.png",
      "created_at": "2016-02-03T02:09:11.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p><span>Hey team I've had some trouble with the Kindle Fire version of SotM and was hoping others here could give me some advice on how to handle it.&nbsp;</span></p><div>&nbsp;</div><div>I purchased the game and the Season 1 pass and have been enjoying playing immensely. My problem occurred when the Shattered Timelines expansion was released. Was told I didn't have enough available space to download and install even with 2 gigs free. Here is the issue as I understand it.&nbsp;</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>(1) Season Pass is its own DLC rather than unlocking the individual DLC so you have to redownload all the previous DLC just to get what's new.&nbsp;</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>(2) Even though you can move apps to a SD card on the Kindle the DLC does not move and takes up space on the internal memory.&nbsp;</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>These two situations combined mean that Sentinels takes up over half the available space on a brand new Fire (I've not installed anything else) and so prevents you from being able to update and the only fix I could find to get Shattered Timelines was to completely uninstall the game and do a fresh install. I'd rather not do that for every update so was hoping to get some advice from other Kindle owners.&nbsp;</div>",
